cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EarlyEval in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "EarlyEval: Cheaper Agent Evaluation via Early Outcome Prediction"
abstract: >-
  EarlyEval is a lightweight framework that reduces the cost of agentic benchmark
  evaluation by predicting a run's final outcome from its partial trajectory. It
  trains a pair of LightGBM success and failure classifiers over behavioral,
  textual, and reference-solution features, and halts an agent run the moment
  either classifier crosses a calibrated confidence threshold.
